Line 27: ## 1. UCC Article 8 terminology --- "Entitlement Order" versus "Instruction"
Line 31: ~~**\[DELETED --- BANK TURN 1\]** "Entitlement Order" is deleted and the operative control language is limited to "Instructions" under Article 9, including the deletion of "Entitlement Orders" from the consent and exclusive-control provisions.~~
Line 33: [**\[ADDED --- PINNACLE TURN 2\]** Section 1 definition and Sections 2.2, 2.4 and 3.2/5.1 are revised to provide that "Entitlement Order" means a notification communicated to Bank directing the transfer, redemption, liquidation or other disposition of a financial asset or interest therein, including an instruction originated by Secured Party. Bank agrees to comply with Instructions and Entitlement Orders originated by Secured Party with respect to the Accounts, without further consent of Depositor. If any Account is at any time deemed a "securities account" under UCC § 8-501, Bank shall treat Secured Party as the entitlement holder and comply with Entitlement Orders originated by Secured Party without further consent of Depositor.]{.underline}
Line 37: ## 2. Springing exclusive control / pre-NOEC account operation
Line 39: **Disposition: Accept ordinary-course operation before an NOEC; reject any qualification of post-NOEC exclusivity.**
Line 41: ~~**\[DELETED --- BANK TURN 1\]** Depositor has a "full and unrestricted" right to issue Instructions before receipt of an NOEC, and Bank has no obligation to inquire into consistency with Loan Documents, Secured Party standing instructions or other arrangements.~~
Line 43: [**\[ADDED --- PINNACLE TURN 2\]** Before Bank's receipt of a Notice of Exclusive Control, Bank may continue to comply with Depositor's Instructions for ordinary-course operation of the Accounts, subject to Secured Party standing limitations and the conflicting-instructions provisions. Upon Bank's receipt of an NOEC, no new Depositor Instruction may be accepted, Depositor's access and instruction rights shall cease without further consent or notice, and Bank shall comply exclusively with Secured Party's Instructions and Entitlement Orders, subject only to the limited processing treatment for items originated and accepted before receipt of the NOEC in Section 5.2.]{.underline}
Line 45: **Negotiation note:** This preserves Graycliff's day-to-day operations while making the springing mechanic crisp. The Bank is not required to determine whether an Event of Default occurred, and the NOEC is not conditioned on Depositor approval, notice or proof.
Line 53: [**\[ADDED --- PINNACLE TURN 2\]** In the event of any conflict among Instructions or Entitlement Orders received from Secured Party, Instructions received from Depositor, and any assertion by Bank of a lien, set-off or recoupment right, the Instructions and Entitlement Orders of Secured Party shall control and prevail. Before an NOEC, Depositor may operate in the ordinary course subject to that priority and prompt conflict notice; upon and after an NOEC, Bank shall comply exclusively with Secured Party's Instructions and Entitlement Orders.]{.underline}
Line 63: [**\[ADDED --- PINNACLE TURN 2\]** Bank may debit the Accounts only for (i) customary, documented account-maintenance, service and transaction fees directly attributable to the Accounts, (ii) returned, reversed, dishonored or charged-back items credited in error or subject to return under applicable law or clearing rules, and (iii) direct, matured, liquidated and undisputed obligations owed by Depositor to Bank arising directly under written deposit-account agreements governing the Accounts, in each case subject to Section 8. No set-off or debit right extends to contingent, unmatured, unliquidated or disputed obligations; any credit facility, loan, letter of credit, treasury-management service unrelated to the Accounts, derivative or swap exposure; or any obligation of an affiliate. Following receipt of an NOEC, no set-off may be exercised except for the limited fees and returned items described above and only in accordance with the subordination provisions.]{.underline}
Line 67: ## 5. NOEC compliance period
Line 71: ~~**\[DELETED --- BANK TURN 1\]** Bank shall comply with an NOEC within five (5) Business Days of receipt.~~
Line 73: [**\[ADDED --- PINNACLE TURN 2\]** Bank shall comply with the NOEC and begin complying exclusively with Secured Party's Instructions and Entitlement Orders no later than the third (3rd) Business Day following Bank's receipt and authentication of the NOEC. No proof, court order, certificate from Depositor or other evidence of an Event of Default shall be required. During the period, Bank may honor only checks, ACH entries, wires or other items originated and accepted before receipt of the NOEC and not yet completed; Bank may not accept new Depositor Instructions after receipt.]{.underline}
Line 77: ## 6. Indemnification / Bank gross negligence
Line 81: ~~**\[DELETED --- BANK TURN 1\]** Secured Party's indemnification applies regardless of whether Losses arise in whole or in part from Bank negligence, including gross negligence, and is limited only to Losses resulting solely and directly from Bank willful misconduct.~~
Line 83: [**\[ADDED --- PINNACLE TURN 2\]** The indemnification obligations of Secured Party and Depositor shall not extend to Losses to the extent finally determined by a court of competent jurisdiction to have resulted from the Bank Indemnitee's gross negligence, willful misconduct, fraud or bad faith, or from Bank's material breach of its representations, warranties, covenants or obligations under this Agreement. The indemnity otherwise applies to good-faith compliance with Secured Party Instructions and performance of the ACA.]{.underline}
Line 85: **Negotiation note:** A secured party should not indemnify a depository bank for the bank's own gross negligence. The carve-out is standard market risk allocation and is a firm client position.
Line 89: **Disposition: Reject and delete the \$50,000 cap in its entirety.**
Line 91: ~~**\[DELETED --- BANK TURN 1\]** Bank's aggregate liability is capped at Fifty Thousand Dollars (\$50,000), subject only to a willful-misconduct exception.~~
Line 95: **Negotiation note:** The cap is not proportionate to the Accounts or the Bank's control obligations. Approximately \$38.15 million is held across the three Accounts; a \$50,000 cap would be de minimis and would eliminate meaningful accountability for a control failure.
Line 111: ~~**\[DELETED --- BANK TURN 1\]** Bank's Liens are subordinated only for fees, charges and returned items incurred during the 90-day period before an NOEC; obligations arising before that period or after the NOEC remain prior and superior.~~
Line 113: [**\[ADDED --- PINNACLE TURN 2\]** Bank subordinates its Liens and set-off rights in the Accounts to Secured Party's Lien with respect to obligations arising during the 180-day period immediately preceding Bank's receipt of the NOEC, except for the limited fees and returned items described in Section 4. Bank may retain only a narrow set-off right for direct, matured, liquidated and undisputed obligations arising directly under written deposit-account agreements and arising before that 180-day period; no right extends to contingent, derivative, affiliate or unrelated credit obligations. No set-off or other Bank Lien for a material obligation may be exercised after receipt of the NOEC.]{.underline}
Line 121: ~~**\[DELETED --- BANK TURN 1\]** Bank may terminate the Agreement in its sole discretion on 30 days' prior written notice, without a successor bank or replacement ACA.~~
Line 123: [**\[ADDED --- PINNACLE TURN 2\]** Bank may terminate this Agreement only upon not less than ninety (90) days' prior written notice to Secured Party and Depositor. During the notice period Bank shall continue to perform all obligations, including compliance with any outstanding NOEC. Secured Party may direct and coordinate the transition of the Accounts to a replacement depository bank, and Depositor shall use commercially reasonable efforts to establish replacement accounts and deliver a replacement ACA reasonably satisfactory to Secured Party. This Agreement shall not terminate until Secured Party confirms in writing that the replacement ACA has been executed and delivered, and Bank shall cooperate with the transition.]{.underline}
Line 129: **Disposition: Reject North Carolina governing law; restore New York law and courts.**
Line 133: [**\[ADDED --- PINNACLE TURN 2\]** This Agreement is governed by the laws of the State of New York, without regard to conflict-of-laws principles that would require application of another jurisdiction's law. Matters relating to perfection, priority and enforcement of security interests in the Accounts remain subject to the applicable UCC jurisdiction under UCC § 9-304. Each Party submits to the exclusive jurisdiction of the United States District Court for the Southern District of New York and the Supreme Court of the State of New York, County of New York (Borough of Manhattan), and appellate courts thereof.]{.underline}
Line 135: **Negotiation note:** New York law is consistent with the Credit Agreement and the other Loan Documents and provides a developed body of law for UCC Articles 8 and 9. The contractual governing-law selection does not displace the UCC's independent rules for perfection and priority.
Line 151: ~~**\[DELETED --- BANK TURN 1\]** The Bank's Turn 1 version deletes the successor-bank notification and assumption provisions.~~
Line 153: [**\[ADDED --- PINNACLE TURN 2\]** Bank shall provide Secured Party at least thirty (30) days' prior written notice of any proposed assignment, transfer, merger, consolidation, succession or transfer of the Accounts or substantially all of Bank's deposit-taking operations that would result in a successor bank. Bank shall cause the successor, to the extent within Bank's control, to assume the ACA in writing and shall remain bound until that assumption and any required replacement control arrangement are delivered. If advance notice is prohibited by applicable law or regulatory order, Bank shall notify Secured Party promptly after it is legally permitted to do so and shall cooperate in obtaining a replacement ACA.]{.underline}
Line 155: **Negotiation note:** Notice is necessary to preserve visibility into the control counterparty and to avoid a perfection gap if the Accounts move to a successor institution. The limited legal/regulatory exception addresses the Bank's stated concern without leaving the ACA silent.
Line 163: [**\[ADDED --- PINNACLE TURN 2\]** Section 11.1 is accepted as written: \$3,500 per Account per annum, \$10,500 annually for the three Accounts. Section 11.2 is revised so that Depositor shall reimburse Bank for reasonable, documented, out-of-pocket external legal fees actually incurred in connection with this Agreement, capped at the lesser of (a) \$7,500 and (b) the amount of such documented fees, payable against an invoice and reasonable supporting detail. No internal personnel time or undocumented amount is reimbursable, and any debit from an Account remains subject to the Secured Party's rights under this Agreement.]{.underline}
Line 169: The following Bank Turn 1 provisions are accepted or should remain, subject to the changes above: (i) completed party names, entity types and bank charter information; (ii) the three-account Schedule A identifying accounts ending 4471, 4472 and 4473 and the approximate balances of \$22.35 million, \$4.18 million and \$11.62 million; (iii) the annual maintenance fee of \$3,500 per account; (iv) the no-proof / no-court-order mechanics for an NOEC; (v) the Depositor indemnification framework, subject to the agreed Secured Party and Bank-fault limitations; (vi) the no-duty-to-monitor and good-faith reliance provisions, subject to the Bank's express obligations under the ACA; and (vii) the mutual jury-trial waiver, electronic execution, severability and entire-agreement provisions.
